<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\ex_{#1}\left[\log\ex_{#1}\left[\exp\left(-\frac{1}{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mu}}\log\frac{d\prob_{\!#1}(\cdot\nonscript\&gt;|\nonscript\&gt;\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}})}{d\prob_{\!#1}(\cdot\nonscript\&gt;|\nonscript\&gt;\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})}\right)\right]\right]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.220em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.387em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.220em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.387em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\ex_{#1}\left[\log\ex_{#1}\left[\exp\left(-\frac{1}{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mu}}\log\frac{d\prob_{\!#1}(\cdot\nonscript\&gt;|\nonscript\&gt;\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}})}{d\prob_{\!#1}(\cdot\nonscript\&gt;|\nonscript\&gt;\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})}\right)\right]\right]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Putting together <a href="#A4.E20" title="In Proof. ‣ D.2 Template Task Selection Bound ‣ Appendix D Task Selection ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.20</span></a>, <a href="#A4.E25" title="Equation D.25 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Template Task Selection Bound ‣ Appendix D Task Selection ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.25</span></a> and <a href="#A4.E27" title="Equation D.27 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Template Task Selection Bound ‣ Appendix D Task Selection ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.27</span></a> concludes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>ICL setting</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us now re-introduce the ICL setting from <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 In-context learning setting ‣ 3 Theoretical framework ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> along with the detailed assumptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\cdot\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\cdot\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Euclidean norm on <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume that task vectors live in <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}\subset{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}}^{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}\subset{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}}^{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}d}</annotation></semantics></math> the space of tasks <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and by <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> the density of the pretraining task distribution.
The context sequence is then generated by first sampling a task <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> from the task distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and then sampling data points <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math> according to</p>
<table id="A4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}+1}\sim\density_{#1}(\cdot\nonscript\,|\nonscript\,\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">p</mi><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}+1}\sim\density_{#1}(\cdot\nonscript\,|\nonscript\,\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(D.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}}=({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}}=({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We denote the posterior <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\widehat{p}}_{#1}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}\nonscript\,|\nonscript\,\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>#</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo fence="false" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\widehat{p}}_{#1}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}\nonscript\,|\nonscript\,\mathopen{}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}-1})</annotation></semantics></math> the posterior distribution over tasks given the input sequence <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1:{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}-1}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#Thmassumption3" title="Assumption 3 (Data generation). ‣ D.3 ICL setting ‣ Appendix D Task Selection ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> combined with <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ D.5 Laplace Approximation ‣ Appendix D Task Selection ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> are the detailed version of <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Data generation, informal). ‣ 3.2 Task selection ‣ 3 Theoretical framework ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> from <a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 In-context learning setting ‣ 3 Theoretical framework ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.
Recall that we write <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\poly(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">poly</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\poly(x)</annotation></semantics></math> to denote a quantity that is polynomial in <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> with coefficients independent of the prior <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of samples <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We also denote by <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\overline{\mathbb{B}}}(0,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔹</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\overline{\mathbb{B}}}(0,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R})</annotation></semantics></math> the closed ball of radius <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R}</annotation></semantics></math> centered at <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}}^{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\mathbb{R}}}^{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}d}</annotation></semantics></math> for the Euclidean norm <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lVert\cdot\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\cdot\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Data generation)<span id="Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}^{*}\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}^{*}\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> the true task and <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}}\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}}\in{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> a reference task such that <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\pi}({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{0}})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ul id="A4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tail behaviour of <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}\geq 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}})_{{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}t}}\geq 1}</annotation></semantics></math>: there is <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R}\geq{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}R}\geq{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
