<p id="A5.Thmlemma8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmlemma8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}c}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}c}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We apply <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem E.1 (Causal symmetrization). ‣ E.1 Moment bounds for general functions ‣ Appendix E Generalization bounds ‣ How Does the Pretraining Distribution Shape In-Context Learning?Task Selection, Generalization, and Robustness" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> with</span></p>
<table id="A5.E99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{m})=({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{1},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1}^{(1)},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}^{(1)},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1}^{({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N})},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}^{({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N})})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Z_{1},\ldots,Z_{m})=({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{1},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1}^{(1)},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}^{(1)},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\theta}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N},{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{1}^{({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N})},\ldots,{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}x}_{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}T}^{({\color[rgb]{0,0,0}N})})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
