<p id="A5.SS3.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}c}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}c}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using Minkowski’s inequality again, we have</span></p>
